    <string name="tutorial_title">Guide</string>
    <string name="tutorial_intro">A quick guide through every part of the app — tap any item to see details.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_main_title">Main screen</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_main_body">Here you see all your medications, vitamins, and supplements. The + button (bottom right) adds a new medication. The magnifier icon scans a box\'s barcode and filters the list if needed. The handset icon opens emergency numbers. The menu (⋮) leads to Appointments, History, Documents, Vitals, and Cycle. The language button (e.g. \"SR\") changes the language instantly, no restart needed.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_addmed_title">Adding and editing a medication</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_addmed_body">Enter the name (or scan the barcode), category (Medication/Vitamin/Supplement), dose and unit, form, and optionally a schedule (every day, specific days, or every X hours) — each time can have its own dose. This is also where you turn on stock tracking and the refill reminder (Premium).</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_history_title">Intake history</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_history_body">A chronological view of every alarm — taken, skipped, or pending. You can manually change the status and search history by date range. Sharing and downloading reports (PDF/CSV) is Premium.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_appointments_title">Appointments</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_appointments_body">Enter a doctor\'s appointment — type of visit, institution, address, date/time, and a reminder before the appointment. The \"Navigation\" button opens Google Maps to the institution\'s address (Premium).</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_documents_title">Reports and lab results</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_documents_body">A chronological archive of photographed results — take a photo with the camera or import from the gallery, add a title and note. View an enlarged image, search by date range. Sharing is Premium.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_vitals_title">Blood pressure and sugar</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_vitals_body">Enter blood pressure readings (systolic/diastolic + pulse) or blood sugar, filter by type. Sharing and downloading (PDF/CSV) are Premium. This is not medical advice.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_cycle_title">Cycle and fertile days</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_cycle_body">Enter the start and end of your cycle; based on the average of previous entries, the app roughly estimates the next cycle and fertile window (at least 2 recorded cycles are needed). Sharing and downloading are Premium. This is only an estimate, not reliable contraception.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_emergency_title">Emergency numbers</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_emergency_body">The 4 basic numbers (police, ambulance, fire, roadside assistance) are filled in automatically based on the app\'s language, and each can also be edited manually — free of charge. Additional, custom numbers (e.g. \"Neighbor\", \"Doctor\") with an icon of your choice are Premium.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_settings_title">Settings</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_settings_body">Choose the app\'s theme (light/dark/system), language, and skin (look) — skins are Premium, and the Custom skin is Premium+. Changes only apply once you tap \"Save changes\". There\'s also a \"Reset settings\" button that restores language/skin/theme to default without deleting your data.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_premium_title">Premium and Premium+</string>
    <string name="tutorial_section_premium_body">Premium unlocks advanced features: skins, sharing/downloading reports, the refill reminder, custom emergency numbers, and navigation to appointments. Premium+ includes everything from Premium and additionally removes the ad at the bottom of the main screen — you get it permanently (test unlock) or temporarily for 1h by watching an ad.</string>
